{
  "id": "Compound::DB00835 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Brompheniramine is implicated in the regulation of arachidonic acid metabolism through its interaction with Cyp2e1 and Cyp2c19, which are both involved in the oxidation of arachidonic acid. The evidence suggests that Brompheniramine binds to Cyp2e1 and Cyp2c19, leading to their participation in the arachidonic acid monooxygenase and epoxygenase activities, respectively. These activities are ultimately linked to Cyp2d6, indicating a potential mechanism by which Brompheniramine influences Cyp2d6 function. The overlapping roles of Cyp2e1 and Cyp2c19 in arachidonic acid metabolism suggest that Brompheniramine may modulate Cyp2d6 through these shared pathways. The consistent scores across the three paths highlight the robustness of this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
